ef67e74230" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060274 #edb/ref 1074 "The function $f(x)$ above is defined for values between $x=-1$ and $x=5.$\n\n- Since there is a closed circle at $x=5,$ this point is included in the domain.\n\n- On the other hand, because there is an open circle at $x=-1,$ this point is not included in the domain.\n\nSo, the function $f(x)$ above is defined for values between $x=-1$ and $x=5,$ including $x=5$ but not including $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nx\\in (-1,5].\n$$\n\nNote that the function is defined at the point $x=3,$  even though the function jumps at that point. The function value at $x=3$ is $1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060463 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060463 #edb/ref 1061 104209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060463 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "271b7b22-3952-5a9c-b297-a12548098709" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060463 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060464 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060464 #edb/ref 1061 104210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060464 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4a1af676-293f-5181-9c71-d019fd78b1fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060464 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060465 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060465 #edb/ref 1061 104213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060465 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a399e495-9b2e-5e32-b85b-e20073c79c2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060465 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060466 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060466 #edb/ref 1061 104216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060466 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ee68356a-78de-58d9-b83a-2af6c68a3a3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060466 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060467 #edb/ref 1061 104219 #edb/r